problem:
Three circular arcs of radius 5 units bound the region shown. Arcs $AB$ and $AD$ are quarter-circles, and arc $BCD$ is a semicircle. What is the area, in square units, of the region? [asy]
/* AMC8 2000 #19 Problem */
draw((0,0)..(1,1)..(2,0));
draw((0,0)..(.7,-.3)..(1,-1));
draw((1,-1)..(1.3, -0.3)..(2,0));
label("$A$", (1,-1), SW);
label("$B$", (0,0), W);
label("$C$", (1,1),N);
label("$D$", (2,0),E);
[/asy]

steps:
Since 5 is relatively prime to 17, there exists a multiplicative inverse of 5 modulo 17. We can find this inverse using the Euclidean Algorithm: \begin{align*}
17 &= 3 \cdot 5 + 2 \\
5 &= 2 \cdot 2 + 1 \\
2 &= 2 \cdot 1.
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
1 &= 5 - 2 \cdot 2 \\
&= 5 - 2(17 - 3 \cdot 5) \\
&= 7 \cdot 5 - 2 \cdot 17.
\end{align*}
